.TH PJ 1 "2026-11-25" "private-journal 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pj \- private, single-user, 2FA-gated encrypted CLI journal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pj
[\fB\-\-help\fR]
[\fB\-\-version\fR]
.I command
[\fIargs...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pj
is a CLI-only encrypted journal. All entry contents, metadata, and file names are encrypted at rest with ChaCha20-Poly1305 using per-file HKDF subkeys derived from an Argon2id Master Key.
.PP
A local Unix-socket session daemon holds the unlocked Master Key in locked memory for a configurable timeout (default 15m). All commands except
.BR unlock ,
.BR lock ,
.BR status ,
and
.BR \-\-help / \-\-version
require an active unlocked session.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B setup [\-\-reset]
Initialize vault password and Google Authenticator TOTP secret. Rejects existing vaults unless \fB\-\-reset\fR is passed and confirmed.
.TP
.B unlock
Verify password and Google Authenticator TOTP code to start or extend the timed session.
.TP
.B lock
Lock immediately, zeroize key buffers, and stop the session daemon.
.TP
.B status
Show current lock state and remaining session timeout.
.TP
.B new [\-\-tag TAG]...
Create a new entry using sandboxed
.BR nvim
(\fB\-n \-i NONE\fR, \fBnobackup\fR, \fBnoundofile\fR, \fBnoswapfile\fR) on a \fB0600\fR temp file in \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR, wiped and deleted on exit.
.TP
.B edit ID [\-\-tag TAG]...
Edit an existing entry in sandboxed
.BR nvim .
.TP
.B view ID
Display a decrypted entry read-only.
.TP
.B delete ID
Delete an encrypted entry.
.TP
.B search [QUERY] [\-\-tag TAG]... [\-\-after YYYY-MM-DD] [\-\-before YYYY-MM-DD] [\-\-plain | \-\-id | \-\-edit]
Search unlocked entries in a transient in-memory index and pick via
.BR fzf
(\fB\-\-no-history\fR). Opens \fBview\fR on selection by default.
.TP
.B config get KEY
Read \fBunlock_timeout\fR or \fBdata_dir\fR.
.TP
.B config set KEY VALUE
Update \fBunlock_timeout\fR or \fBdata_dir\fR.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/private-journal/config.json
User configuration (\fB0600\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/private-journal/
Vault metadata (\fBvault.json\fR) and encrypted entries (\fBentries/*.enc\fR).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/private-journal/daemon.sock
Local \fB0600\fR Unix domain socket for the active session daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nvim (1),
.BR fzf (1)
